{{- /* internal/render/templates/index.gohtml — the submissions index
(§7.2): one row per submission, ordinal/profile/verdict/assessment/
severity in fixed CSS-grid columns (styling is bead .5's; this file only
supplies structure and class names), never collapsed — same
first-thing-a-reader-needs reasoning as templates/envelope.gohtml, so
never behind a <details> either.

Dot is htmlEnvelopeView (internal/render/html_view_envelope.go); .Submissions
is the per-submission row data. An empty .Submissions — the store has
nothing for this ref, or the ref has zero submissions — renders the
explicit "no submissions found for this ref" empty state instead of a
grid with nothing in it (§12), still inside the same page structure so a
zero-submission run is a well-formed page, not a blank one.

Each row's ordinal doubles as the link into the findings section (§7.2:
the index is what a reader scans first to decide where to go), via
fragmentHref (html_href.go, §8.2-8.3) — the same helper, called the same
way, templates/finding.gohtml already uses for a finding's own permalink.
FindingID is "" for a submission that filed no comments, so that row's
ordinal renders as plain text rather than a link to nowhere.

Two fields beyond the five grid columns (refinery-t1c.4): every row is
immediately followed by its own full-width "index-summary-row" carrying
Summary, unconditionally, the same way markdown.go's
writeMarkdownSubmissions always writes the indented summary paragraph
below its bullet regardless of length — 30-1500 characters of prose is
the wrong shape for a fixed grid cell, so it gets its own row instead of
a sixth column. A row whose HasSupersededBy is true instead gets an
"index-row-superseded" class, muting its own cells, plus a small tag in
the ordinal cell naming the ordinal that superseded it — placed first,
before profile/verdict/assessment/severity, because a reader has to know
a row is stale before reading the rest of it, not after. Both rows —
row and its summary — share the same grid container as the header and
data rows above them: "index-summary-row" reaches full width with
grid-column: 1/-1, the identical mechanism report.css's own ".index-row"
already uses, declared in the <style> block below rather than in
report.css itself, the same "a partial owns a few rules of its own
presentation, reusing report.css's custom properties, without editing
that file" pattern templates/toolbar.gohtml already establishes for the
identical reason: bead .5's ownership of report.css stays untouched. */ -}}
{{define "index"}}
<section id="submissions" class="submissions">
{{if .Submissions}}
<div class="index" role="table">
<style>
.index-row-superseded .index-cell { color: var(--text-muted); }
.index-superseded-tag {
  margin-left: 0.4rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--chip-border);
  background: var(--chip-bg);
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-weight: 600;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.02em;
}
.index-summary-row { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
.index-summary-row .index-summary {
  display: block;
  padding: 0.35rem 0.75rem 0.75rem;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  white-space: pre-wrap;
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}
</style>
<div class="index-row index-header" role="row">
<span class="index-cell" role="columnheader">#</span>
<span class="index-cell" role="columnheader">profile</span>
<span class="index-cell" role="columnheader">verdict</span>
<span class="index-cell" role="columnheader">assessment</span>
<span class="index-cell" role="columnheader">severity</span>
</div>
{{range .Submissions}}
<div class="index-row{{if .HasSupersededBy}} index-row-superseded{{end}}" role="row">
<span class="index-cell index-ordinal" role="cell">{{if .FindingID}}<a href="#{{fragmentHref .FindingID}}">#{{.Ordinal}}</a>{{else}}#{{.Ordinal}}{{end}}{{if .HasSupersededBy}} <span class="tag index-superseded-tag" title="superseded by submission #{{.SupersededBy}}">superseded by #{{.SupersededBy}}</span>{{end}}</span>
<span class="index-cell index-profile" role="cell">{{.Profile}}</span>
<span class="index-cell index-verdict" role="cell">{{.Verdict}}</span>
<span class="index-cell index-assessment" role="cell">{{.Assessment}}</span>
<span class="index-cell index-severity" role="cell">{{.Severity}}</span>
</div>
<div class="index-summary-row" role="row">
<span class="index-cell index-summary" role="cell">{{.Summary}}</span>
</div>
{{end}}
</div>
{{else}}
<p class="empty-state">no submissions found for this ref</p>
{{end}}
</section>
{{end}}
